1
00:00:02,438 --> 00:00:05,565
Water, earth,

2
00:00:06,985 --> 00:00:09,945
fire, air...

3
00:00:11,239 --> 00:00:14,574
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

4
00:00:15,285 --> 00:00:18,495
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

5
00:00:19,664 --> 00:00:20,914
Only the Avatar,

6
00:00:20,999 --> 00:00:22,582
master of all four elements,

7
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:23,709
could stop them.

8
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:25,544
But when the world needed him most,

9
00:00:25,628 --> 00:00:26,920
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,338 --> 00:00:30,507
100 years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

11
00:00:31,259 --> 00:00:32,926
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:33,011 --> 00:00:35,095
And although his
airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,179 --> 00:00:38,598
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:39,017 --> 00:00:41,893
But I believe Aang can save the world.

15
00:01:03,666 --> 00:01:05,125
-Yay! Yay!
-Aang's back!

16
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:15,052
I knew it.

17
00:01:15,136 --> 00:01:17,262
You signaled the Fire Navy
with that flare.

18
00:01:17,555 --> 00:01:19,598
You're leading them
straight to us, aren't you?

19
00:01:19,682 --> 00:01:21,016
Aang didn't do anything.

20
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:22,601
It was an accident.

21
00:01:22,685 --> 00:01:24,102
Yeah, we were on the ship

22
00:01:24,187 --> 00:01:25,187
and there was this booby trap,

23
00:01:25,271 --> 00:01:27,064
and, well, we--

24
00:01:27,148 --> 00:01:28,482
We boobied right into it.

25
00:01:28,733 --> 00:01:31,401
Katara, you shouldn't have
gone on that ship.

26
00:01:31,694 --> 00:01:33,528
Now we could all be in danger.

27
00:01:33,863 --> 00:01:35,030
Don't blame Katara.

28
00:01:35,114 --> 00:01:36,698
I brought her there.

29
00:01:36,908 --> 00:01:37,908
It's my fault.

30
00:01:37,992 --> 00:01:38,992
A-ha!

31
00:01:39,077 --> 00:01:40,452
The traitor confesses!

32
00:01:40,828 --> 00:01:42,621
Warriors, away from the enemy!

33
00:01:42,705 --> 00:01:45,082
The foreigner is banished
from our village.

34
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:47,417
Sokka, you're making a mistake.

35
00:01:47,627 --> 00:01:49,753
No, I'm keeping my promise to dad.

36
00:01:49,962 --> 00:01:51,797
I'm protecting you
from threats like him.

37
00:01:52,006 --> 00:01:54,049
Aang is not our enemy.

38
00:01:54,258 --> 00:01:55,801
Don't you see?

39
00:01:56,010 --> 00:01:57,260
Aang's brought us something

40
00:01:57,345 --> 00:02:00,180
we haven't had in a long time-- Fun.

41
00:02:00,431 --> 00:02:03,183
Fun? We can't fight firebenders
with fun!

42
00:02:03,684 --> 00:02:05,102
You should try it sometime.

43
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:07,479
Get out of our village, now!

44
00:02:07,855 --> 00:02:10,982
Grandmother, please,
don't let Sokka do this.

45
00:02:11,192 --> 00:02:13,985
Katara, you knew going on
that ship was forbidden.

46
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:15,654
Sokka is right.

47
00:02:15,738 --> 00:02:18,323
I think it best
if the airbender leaves.

48
00:02:18,658 --> 00:02:21,243
Fine, then I'm banished, too.

49
00:02:21,327 --> 00:02:22,911
Come on, Aang, let's go.

50
00:02:23,663 --> 00:02:25,288
Where do you think you're going?

51
00:02:25,498 --> 00:02:27,040
To find a waterbender.

52
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:29,418
Aang is taking me to the North Pole.

53
00:02:30,294 --> 00:02:31,294
I am?

54
00:02:31,379 --> 00:02:33,004
- Great!
- Katara!

55
00:02:33,548 --> 00:02:35,882
Would you really choose him
over your tribe,

56
00:02:36,384 --> 00:02:37,634
your own family?

57
00:02:43,766 --> 00:02:46,685
Katara, I don't want to come between
you and your family.

58
00:02:49,021 --> 00:02:51,815
So you're leaving the South Pole?

59
00:02:52,442 --> 00:02:53,733
This is goodbye?

60
00:02:54,068 --> 00:02:55,735
Thanks for penguin sledding with me.

61
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:57,279
Where will you go?

62
00:02:57,363 --> 00:02:59,906
Guess I'll go back home
and look for the airbenders.

63
00:03:00,658 --> 00:03:01,867
Wow.

64
00:03:01,951 --> 00:03:04,161
I haven't cleaned my room
in 100 years.

65
00:03:04,662 --> 00:03:06,079
Not looking forward to that.

66
00:03:09,876 --> 00:03:11,334
It was nice meeting everyone.

67
00:03:11,669 --> 00:03:14,713
Let's see your bison fly now, Airboy.

68
00:03:14,797 --> 00:03:16,715
Come on, Appa, you can do it.

69
00:03:17,049 --> 00:03:18,049
Yip yip!

70
00:03:20,803 --> 00:03:21,970
Yeah, I thought so!

71
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:26,725
Aang, don't go.

72
00:03:26,809 --> 00:03:27,976
I'll miss you.

73
00:03:28,686 --> 00:03:29,936
I'll miss you, too.

74
00:03:35,359 --> 00:03:36,693
Come on, boy.

75
00:03:46,078 --> 00:03:48,747
Katara, you'll feel better after you--

76
00:03:48,831 --> 00:03:50,081
You happy now?

77
00:03:50,166 --> 00:03:53,335
There goes my one chance
of becoming a waterbender!

78
00:03:58,758 --> 00:04:00,550
All right, ready our defenses!

79
00:04:00,635 --> 00:04:02,928
The Fire Nation could be
on our shores any moment now!

80
00:04:03,012 --> 00:04:04,054
But I got to--

81
00:04:04,138 --> 00:04:05,597
And no potty breaks!

82
00:04:18,236 --> 00:04:20,278
Yeah, I liked her, too.

83
00:04:27,995 --> 00:04:28,995
The village!

84
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:35,877
Appa, wait here!

85
00:05:42,987 --> 00:05:44,571
Man!

86
00:05:53,789 --> 00:05:54,956
Man.

87
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,852
Sokka! Get out of the way!

88
00:07:29,719 --> 00:07:30,969
Where are you hiding him?

89
00:07:38,519 --> 00:07:40,228
He'd be about this age,

90
00:07:40,312 --> 00:07:42,230
master of all elements.

91
00:07:51,657 --> 00:07:52,991
I know you're hiding him.

92
00:08:05,755 --> 00:08:07,505
Show no fear!

93
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:56,596
Hey, Katara. Hey, Sokka.

94
00:08:56,806 --> 00:08:58,348
Hi, Aang.

95
00:08:58,432 --> 00:08:59,432
Thanks for coming.

96
00:09:14,532 --> 00:09:15,824
Looking for me?

97
00:09:15,908 --> 00:09:17,784
You're the airbender?

98
00:09:18,285 --> 00:09:20,411
You're the Avatar?

99
00:09:21,205 --> 00:09:22,205
Aang?

100
00:09:22,289 --> 00:09:23,289
No way.

101
00:09:26,544 --> 00:09:29,504
I've spent years preparing
for this encounter,

102
00:09:29,588 --> 00:09:31,756
training, meditating.

103
00:09:32,049 --> 00:09:34,050
You're just a child.

104
00:09:34,134 --> 00:09:35,343
Well, you're just a teenager.

105
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,526
If I go with you,

106
00:09:51,610 --> 00:09:53,403
will you promise
to leave everyone alone?

107
00:10:03,914 --> 00:10:05,790
No, Aang, don't do this.

108
00:10:06,417 --> 00:10:07,542
Don't worry, Katara.

109
00:10:07,626 --> 00:10:09,711
It'll be ok.

110
00:10:09,795 --> 00:10:10,795
Unh!

111
00:10:13,883 --> 00:10:16,509
Take care of Appa for me
until I get back.

112
00:10:16,594 --> 00:10:18,553
Head a course to the Fire Nation.

113
00:10:18,637 --> 00:10:20,013
I'm going home.

114
00:10:59,970 --> 00:11:02,096
We have to go after that ship, Sokka.

115
00:11:02,181 --> 00:11:03,598
Aang saved our tribe.

116
00:11:03,682 --> 00:11:05,099
Now we have to save him.

117
00:11:05,184 --> 00:11:06,267
Katara, I--

118
00:11:06,352 --> 00:11:08,269
Why can't you realize
that he's on our side?

119
00:11:08,604 --> 00:11:10,563
If we don't help him, no one will.

120
00:11:10,648 --> 00:11:12,857
I know you don't like Aang,
but we owe him and--

121
00:11:12,942 --> 00:11:15,234
Katara, are you going to talk all day

122
00:11:15,319 --> 00:11:16,819
or are you coming with me?

123
00:11:17,905 --> 00:11:18,947
Sokka!

124
00:11:21,075 --> 00:11:22,075
Get in.

125
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:23,326
We're going to save your boyfriend.

126
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:24,702
-He's not my--
-Whatever.

127
00:11:25,537 --> 00:11:27,372
What do you two think you're doing?

128
00:11:29,333 --> 00:11:31,125
You'll need these.

129
00:11:31,335 --> 00:11:33,503
You have a long journey ahead of you.

130
00:11:36,298 --> 00:11:39,425
It's been so long since I've had hope,

131
00:11:39,718 --> 00:11:41,427
but you brought it back to life,

132
00:11:41,512 --> 00:11:42,553
my little waterbender.

133
00:11:44,932 --> 00:11:47,558
And you, my brave warrior,

134
00:11:47,768 --> 00:11:49,602
be nice to your sister.

135
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:52,689
Yeah, ok, Gran.

136
00:11:53,482 --> 00:11:55,024
Aang is the Avatar.

137
00:11:55,109 --> 00:11:57,318
He's the world's only chance.

138
00:11:57,403 --> 00:11:59,696
You both found him for a reason.

139
00:12:00,114 --> 00:12:03,533
Now your destinies
are intertwined with his.

140
00:12:05,953 --> 00:12:07,286
There's no way we're going to catch

141
00:12:07,371 --> 00:12:09,163
a warship with a canoe.

142
00:12:13,210 --> 00:12:14,293
Appa!

143
00:12:14,378 --> 00:12:16,337
You just love taking me
out of my comfort zone,

144
00:12:16,422 --> 00:12:17,422
don't you?

145
00:12:23,095 --> 00:12:26,472
This staff will make
an excellent gift for my father.

146
00:12:26,557 --> 00:12:28,599
I suppose you wouldn't
know of fathers,

147
00:12:28,684 --> 00:12:30,685
being raised by monks.

148
00:12:31,311 --> 00:12:33,229
Take the Avatar to the prison hold

149
00:12:33,313 --> 00:12:34,856
and take this to my quarters.

150
00:12:36,734 --> 00:12:39,694
Hey, you mind taking this
to his quarters for me?

151
00:12:55,085 --> 00:12:58,546
So, I guess you've never fought
an airbender before.

152
00:12:58,630 --> 00:13:00,131
I bet I can take you both

153
00:13:00,215 --> 00:13:01,674
with my hands tied behind my back.

154
00:13:01,759 --> 00:13:02,759
Silence.

155
00:13:22,738 --> 00:13:23,988
The Avatar has escaped!

156
00:13:31,038 --> 00:13:32,038
Go.

157
00:13:32,498 --> 00:13:33,623
Fly.

158
00:13:33,707 --> 00:13:35,083
Soar.

159
00:13:36,085 --> 00:13:38,127
Please, Appa, we need your help.

160
00:13:38,212 --> 00:13:39,420
Aang needs your help.

161
00:13:39,505 --> 00:13:40,505
Up.

162
00:13:40,589 --> 00:13:42,006
Ascend.

163
00:13:42,091 --> 00:13:43,216
Elevate.

164
00:13:44,218 --> 00:13:46,010
Sokka doesn't believe you can fly,

165
00:13:46,386 --> 00:13:47,929
But I do, Appa.

166
00:13:48,013 --> 00:13:50,014
Come on, don't you want to save Aang?

167
00:13:53,143 --> 00:13:54,602
What was it that kid said?

168
00:13:54,728 --> 00:13:55,728
Yee-ha?

169
00:13:55,813 --> 00:13:56,813
Hup-hup?

170
00:13:56,897 --> 00:13:57,897
Wa-hoo?

171
00:13:58,315 --> 00:14:00,108
Yip yip?

172
00:14:10,119 --> 00:14:11,410
You did it, Sokka!

173
00:14:12,329 --> 00:14:14,455
He's flying!

174
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,541
Katara, he's--

175
00:14:17,751 --> 00:14:19,085
I mean, big deal.

176
00:14:19,169 --> 00:14:20,211
He's flying.

177
00:14:30,889 --> 00:14:31,889
Aah!

178
00:14:33,267 --> 00:14:35,143
You haven't seen
my staff around, have you?

179
00:14:41,650 --> 00:14:42,650
Thanks, anyway.

180
00:15:07,676 --> 00:15:08,718
Sorry.

181
00:15:16,018 --> 00:15:17,018
My staff!

182
00:15:18,770 --> 00:15:20,438
Looks like I underestimated you.

183
00:16:56,201 --> 00:16:57,243
What is that?

184
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:01,580
Appa!

185
00:17:22,769 --> 00:17:24,145
Aang, no!

186
00:17:26,356 --> 00:17:28,607
Aang! Aang!

187
00:17:29,276 --> 00:17:30,401
Aang!

188
00:17:57,804 --> 00:17:59,347
Did you see what he just did?

189
00:17:59,431 --> 00:18:01,891
Now that was some waterbending.

190
00:18:10,525 --> 00:18:12,735
Aang, are you ok?

191
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:16,405
Hey, Katara.

192
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:17,698
Hey, Sokka.

193
00:18:17,783 --> 00:18:19,033
Thanks for coming.

194
00:18:19,117 --> 00:18:21,410
Well, I couldn't let you
have all the glory.

195
00:18:21,828 --> 00:18:23,162
I dropped my staff.

196
00:18:23,246 --> 00:18:24,372
Got it.

197
00:18:35,675 --> 00:18:36,675
Ha!

198
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:38,010
That's from the water tribe!

199
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:49,230
Katara!

200
00:19:00,951 --> 00:19:02,201
Hurry up, Sokka!

201
00:19:02,285 --> 00:19:04,036
I'm just a guy with a boomerang.

202
00:19:04,121 --> 00:19:06,914
I didn't ask for all this
flying and magic.

203
00:19:08,458 --> 00:19:09,500
Yip yip! Yip yip!

204
00:19:22,055 --> 00:19:23,055
Shoot them down!

205
00:19:48,999 --> 00:19:50,916
Good news for the Fire Lord.

206
00:19:51,001 --> 00:19:53,836
The Fire Nation's greatest threat

207
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,337
is just a little kid.

208
00:19:55,797 --> 00:19:58,757
That kid, uncle, just did this.

209
00:19:59,176 --> 00:20:01,177
I won't underestimate him again.

210
00:20:01,678 --> 00:20:03,429
Dig this ship out and follow them.

211
00:20:06,725 --> 00:20:07,850
As soon as you're done with that.

212
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:17,443
How did you
do that with the water?

213
00:20:17,527 --> 00:20:19,945
It was the most amazing thing
I've ever seen.

214
00:20:20,447 --> 00:20:21,489
I don't know.

215
00:20:21,573 --> 00:20:23,324
I just sort of did it.

216
00:20:24,326 --> 00:20:27,328
Why didn't you tell us
you were the Avatar?

217
00:20:27,829 --> 00:20:30,581
Because I never wanted to be.

218
00:20:41,092 --> 00:20:44,345
But, Aang, the world's been waiting
for the Avatar to return

219
00:20:44,429 --> 00:20:46,639
and finally put an end to this war.

220
00:20:47,057 --> 00:20:48,891
And how am I going to do that?

221
00:20:49,017 --> 00:20:50,226
According to legend,

222
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:52,186
You need to first master water,

223
00:20:52,270 --> 00:20:54,271
then earth, then fire, right?

224
00:20:54,356 --> 00:20:55,773
That's what the monks told me.

225
00:20:55,857 --> 00:20:57,858
Well, if we go to the north pole,

226
00:20:57,943 --> 00:20:59,902
you can master waterbending.

227
00:20:59,986 --> 00:21:01,320
We could learn it together!

228
00:21:01,821 --> 00:21:03,906
And, Sokka,
I'm sure you'll get to knock

229
00:21:03,990 --> 00:21:05,616
some firebender heads on the way.

230
00:21:05,909 --> 00:21:06,951
I'd like that.

231
00:21:07,035 --> 00:21:08,494
I'd really like that.

232
00:21:09,162 --> 00:21:10,871
Then we're in this together.

233
00:21:10,956 --> 00:21:12,915
All right,
but before I learn waterbending,

234
00:21:12,999 --> 00:21:15,584
we have some
serious business to attend to

235
00:21:15,669 --> 00:21:18,045
here, here, and here.

236
00:21:18,129 --> 00:21:19,713
What's there?

237
00:21:19,798 --> 00:21:21,882
Here we'll ride the hopping llamas.

238
00:21:21,967 --> 00:21:25,052
Then way over here we'll surf
on the backs of giant koi fish.

239
00:21:25,387 --> 00:21:27,888
Then back over here
we'll ride the hog monkeys.

240
00:21:28,139 --> 00:21:29,765
They don't like people riding them,

241
00:21:29,849 --> 00:21:31,267
but that's what makes it fun!
